"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":0.6,"y":0.0,"z":0.24}],"uuid":"186f25b2-21b7-5630-abf1-6bbba7b99186","time":0.16,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":-0.3,"y":0.0,"z":-0.12}],"uuid":"db47ee53-d4df-578a-ae9d-0708516b107c","time":0.22,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"1c46a02c-8f5d-5a3b-aea0-71b8cd321c5e","time":0.3,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"}]},"2795dd00-c41a-5f96-92b8-764e488682b7":{"name":"depleted","type":"bone","keyframes":[{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"e83326dc-0829-5dac-b747-4850612d4037","time":0,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":1.2,"y":0.0,"z":0.48}],"uuid":"dd70f5ad-e8ad-59c9-84df-cb61ee4bb49d","time":0.04,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":-1.0,"y":0.0,"z":-0.4}],"uuid":"56974fce-0885-5e3e-a6d9-2037ef777e5a","time":0.1,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":0.6,"y":0.0,"z":0.24}],"uuid":"f4cd0e46-f412-5361-98e3-b96363caf53d","time":0.16,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":-0.3,"y":0.0,"z":-0.12}],"uuid":"e272dc8b-8347-5f4d-a6d6-c34504f68b4f","time":0.22,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"f7f3a4c5-7c9b-5614-b521-44b1513738e4","time":0.3,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"}]}}}],"description":"# rock_lead\n\nLead node: grey-blue rock with dull silvery lumps.\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -43..53, y 0..39, z -34..30 units (2.70 x 1.10 x 1.80 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 128 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering; every visible face has its own region painted with its material at world position (identical faces share one). No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: 22.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 96 x 39 x 64 (w x h x d), centred at x 5, z -2\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `full` (visible by default): untouched node; the child group `companion` is the paler silver-grey rock that often sits beside it (hide it if the game places silver separately)\n- `depleted`: mined out: smaller broken chunks and gravel\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `hit` | 0.3 | once | short shake when struck (both sets) |\n"}